   "html_text": "This is a visual argument because it depends on visual meanings (conveyed with an NL+ rather than a mere NL). The verbal paraphrase summarizes the apparent logic of the argument, though the non-verbal visual elements leave open the possibility of further interpretation. Notably, the Napoleon-III-as-porcupine caricature may be an allusion to a different “Louis” King of France–to Louis XII, who ruled from 1498 to 1515. On this interpretation, the argument claims that Napoleon III is acting like Lo",
